          "Kyle's 1985 market microstructure framework formalizes price formation around three agents: a single informed trader holding private fundamental value, noise traders creating random uncorrelated flow, and a risk-neutral market maker setting clearing prices solely from aggregate net order flow `Q`. Because net flow correlates with private information, prices adjust linearly with signed order flow.",
