          "Step 2 passes those exact residuals into `test_residual_cointegration(residuals, adf_t_stat)`. Standard Dickey-Fuller critical tables assume known variables rather than estimated `alpha` and `beta`; estimating two parameters in-sample fits residuals artificially tightly, so Engle-Granger requires stricter MacKinnon critical values (`-3.37` at 5% significance).",
          "Checking `adf_t_stat < -3.37` rejects the unit-root null hypothesis cleanly, returning `COINTEGRATED_PAIR_CERTIFIED` alongside `cointegrated: True`. Any `adf_t_stat` less negative than `-3.37` indicates residuals could still wander permanently like a random walk (`NO_COINTEGRATION`).",
