          "The Fundamental Law of Active Management, formulated by Richard Grinold and Ronald Kahn, provides quantitative investment teams with an analytical identity connecting forecasting skill, portfolio decision breadth, and realized risk-adjusted excess return. Rather than judging strategies blindly on historical backtest curves, allocators decompose Information Ratio into independent measurable drivers.",
