          "Inspect both structural drivers mathematically inside `FundamentalLawFoundations.compute_classical_ir(ic, breadth)`. Even a remarkably skilled fundamental analyst posting `IC = 0.20` on only `4` concentrated quarterly stock picks per year achieves `IR = 0.20 * sqrt(4) = 0.40`, trailing systematic strategies carrying modest skill across broad opportunity sets.",
