          "Rounding option prices carefully (`round(val, 4)`) protects sub-penny institutional spreads while keeping Put-Call checks transparent in audit logs.",
          "Understanding why no-arbitrage synthetic forwards lock call and put prices together explains how options desks hedge spot exposure cleanly across strikes. Deriving continuous no-arbitrage fair prices via `BSMFoundations.call_put_price` (`Call: USD 10.4506 | Put: USD 5.5735 | Parity: True` at `S=100, K=100, T=1.0, r=0.05, sigma=0.20`) converts directional equity guesses into exact replicating portfolio mathematics. Under continuous delta hedging, option values depend only on observable spot price, strike, interest rate, time to maturity, and future volatility—notice that the underlying stock's expected growth drift drops clean out of the PDE completely! Implementing cumulative standard normal probabilities directly via pure standard-library `math.erf` (`0.5 * (1 + erf(x / sqrt(2)))`) gives lightweight derivatives desks deterministic `1e-15` double precision with zero heavyweight external binary dependencies. Quantitative validation suites guard expiry boundary singularities safely (`t <= 0 or sigma <= 0` snapping cleanly onto intrinsic payoffs without divide-by-zero exceptions), verify Put-Call Parity identity within machine tolerance across skewed strikes and dividend yields, confirm non-negativity above lower bounds (`C >= max(0, S - K*e^-rT)`), and check deep ITM/OTM asymptotics cleanly. Evaluating European option valuation under the Black-Scholes-Merton framework requires enforcing no-arbitrage boundaries before downstream Greek desks consume any price curve. When the foundations module computes a call price of `10.4506` USD and a corresponding put price of `5.5735` USD across identical strike, maturity, rate, and spot parameters, verifying put-call parity (`Parity: True`) guards against sign inversions in discounting factors. In multi-currency or dividend-adjusted desks, storing continuous yield and risk-free rate conventions inside an immutable valuation context prevents silent basis drift between pricing runs. Regression suites check both at-the-money symmetry and deep in-the-money discounting limits so `BSMFoundations` catches numerical instability prior to production surface bootstrapping.",
