          "Notice explicit zero-exception corner handling (`if x == 0`): avoiding `0 * ln(0)` undefined terms simplifies null probability smoothly to `-2 * math.log((1 - p) ** n)`, whereas standard `x > 0` paths compute exact `num / den` guarded against underflow cleanly (`else 999.0`).",
          "Under the null hypothesis that the VaR engine models tail risk accurately, Kupiec's `LR` statistic follows a Chi-squared distribution with `1` degree of freedom (`95%` confidence bound = `3.841`). Checking `is_accepted = lr_stat <= 3.841` validates (`MODEL_VALIDATED`) or rejects (`MODEL_REJECTED_UNDERESTIMATED_RISK`) the engine cleanly!",
